From: HaeImAlan <me@haeimalan.com>
Date: Sat, 13 Sep 2026 10:01:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: shrink the WBM link descriptor pool in the 256M profile

The WBM idle link descriptor pool is sized in ath11k_wbm_idle_ring_setup()
from DP_NUM_CLIENTS_MAX, DP_AVG_MPDUS_PER_TID_MAX and friends, rounded up
to a power of two. The default constants give 18560 -> 32768 descriptors
of 128 bytes, i.e. 4 MB of DMA memory per ath11k_base plus a 256 KB
(512 KB after page-order rounding) WBM idle ring. This pool is not
covered by the QSDK profiles, which keep 4 MB even at 256M.

In the 256M profile the firmware is limited to 128 peers per radio and
the RX side holds at most 1024 buffers, so the 128 MPDUs-per-TID budget is
oversized. Lowering DP_AVG_MPDUS_PER_TID_MAX to 32 gives 8149 -> 8192
descriptors: 1 MB of pool and a 64 KB idle ring, saving ~3.4 MB per
radio. DP_NUM_CLIENTS_MAX is left at 64 so that the per-client TX MSDU
link descriptor budget (which does not depend on the MPDU count) is
unchanged.

Signed-off-by: HaeImAlan <me@haeimalan.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h
@@ -191,7 +191,15 @@
 #define DP_NUM_TIDS_MAX (DP_NUM_CLIENTS_MAX * DP_AVG_TIDS_PER_CLIENT)
 #define DP_AVG_MSDUS_PER_FLOW 128
 #define DP_AVG_FLOWS_PER_TID 2
+/* Per-TID MPDU budget feeding the WBM link descriptor pool size. 128 gives
+ * a 4 MB pool (32768 descriptors); 32 gives 1 MB (8192 descriptors),
+ * which is plenty for 128 peers and 1024 RX buffers per radio.
+ */
+#if defined(CPTCFG_ATH11K_MEM_PROFILE_256M)
+#define DP_AVG_MPDUS_PER_TID_MAX 32
+#else
 #define DP_AVG_MPDUS_PER_TID_MAX 128
+#endif
 #define DP_AVG_MSDUS_PER_MPDU 4
 
 #define DP_RX_HASH_ENABLE	1 /* Enable hash based Rx steering */
